OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G1/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,FA full profile for voiceover artist Jon
OL,7,FBriggs can be found on The TV Room's
OL,8,FShowreel website.
OL,10,FPaul R. Jackson corresponded with Jon
OL,11,Fin July 2025 about his long
OL,12,Fbroadcasting career.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G2/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID YOU GET INTO BROADCASTING AND
OL,7,GWAS BBC RADIO OXFORD YOUR FIRST JOB?
OL,9,F"Yes, Radio Oxford was my first media
OL,10,Fjob. I blagged my way in and nagged
OL,11,Fthem to let me have a go. Eventually
OL,12,Fthey caved in and I became the tea boy
OL,13,Fmade good!
OL,15,F"Starting on air with Timmy Mallett `
OL,16,Fwriting and voicing Mr Wiggleknuckle `
OL,17,Fthe useless salesman from Trannyoid
OL,18,FProducts in April 1982 (while still at
OL,19,Fschool). I was given my own show the
OL,20,Fsummer I left school in 1983 ` leaving
OL,21,Fin 1989.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14403
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G3/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"With a brief stint on Saturday
OL,7,Fmornings when I was invited back as you
OL,8,Fidentify above."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14404
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G4/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID THE MOVE FROM LOCAL RADIO TO
OL,7,GNETWORK RADIO COME ABOUT?
OL,9,F"I applied for the advertised job as
OL,10,Freporter on The Chip Shop.
OL,12,F"Barry Norman was the presenter and it
OL,13,Fwas the BBC's first foray into IT.
OL,15,F"Radio 5 was just a case of badgering
OL,16,Fthe editor Gaynor Vaughan-Jones, until
OL,17,Fshe got me in for an audition."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14405
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G5/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID YOU GET TO JOIN BBC RADIO 5
OL,7,GAND WHAT ARE YOUR MEMORIES OF BEING
OL,8,GTHE LAUNCH CO-PRESENTER ON MORNING
OL,9,GEDITION AND WORKING WITH LEGENDARY
OL,10,GBROADCASTER SARAH WARD?
OL,12,F"Morning Edition was a great programme.
OL,14,F"However the BBC didn't like this young
OL,15,Fupstart that had created a hybrid
OL,16,Fbetween studio managers and producers `
OL,17,Fpeople who created the programmes and
OL,18,Fwould also be the tech ops for them.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14406
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G6/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Coming from local radio, where you did
OL,7,Feverything, it all made perfect sense
OL,8,Fto me ` but it made a big hole in the
OL,9,Funion set up in BH.
OL,11,F"So, we didn't get given any of the
OL,12,FRadio 4 correspondents when trying to
OL,13,Fcover the first Gulf War. So we created
OL,14,Four own list of journalists that would
OL,15,Freport for us ` people that
OL,16,Fsubsequently went on to work for R4 and
OL,17,Fmany other outlets of the BBC as they
OL,18,Fwere so good.
OL,20,F"So, we had to be highly creative to
OL,21,Fprovide a breakfast news service.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14407
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G7/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Sarah and I didn't really see eye to
OL,7,Feye. There was a significant age
OL,8,Fdifference, but we found a way to work
OL,9,Ftogether.
OL,11,F"We were never close friends, however,
OL,12,Fand I enjoyed the Saturday morning show
OL,13,Fmore as it was my own ` in fact the
OL,14,FUK's first sports breakfast show as
OL,15,Fthat's what we concentrated on."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14408
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G8/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID YOU MOVE INTO PRESENTATION AND
OL,7,GWHO WERE YOUR ANNOUNCER COLLEAGUES ON
OL,8,GRADIO 1 AND RADIO 2?
OL,10,F"The move into Pres was partly because
OL,11,FI had been offered a job at the end of
OL,12,FThe Chip Shop in Radio 4 Pres.
OL,14,F"But at the same time I was offered the
OL,15,Fbreakfast show back in Oxford. Aged 20
OL,16,FI wanted to be on a breakfast show, so
OL,17,Ftook that. How things could have been
OL,18,Fso different!
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14409
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G9/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"R4 Pres didn't like me much ` Peter
OL,7,FDonaldson hauled me over the coals for
OL,8,Freading the Haitian capital with a
OL,9,FFrench pronunciation of Port au Prince
OL,10,F` and I never read news for R4 again
OL,11,Fbut did continue in the continuity
OL,12,Fbooth.
OL,14,F"Peter was not the cuddly old codger
OL,15,Fthat many people talk about.
OL,17,F"As I had read the news bulletins for
OL,18,FRadio 5 during the breakfast show and
OL,19,Fthen stayed on to read the rest of them
OL,20,Funtil midday, it was an easy move to
OL,21,Fread for Radios 1, 2 and 4.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14410
SC,0010
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G10/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I read again for Radio 5 Live in the
OL,7,Fearly 2000s when the station was based
OL,8,Fat TVC."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14411
SC,0011
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G11/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GWHAT DATES DID YOU WORK AT LBC AND
OL,7,GWHAT PROGRAMMES DID YOU PRESENT?
OL,9,F"I started sitting in for Frank Bough
OL,10,Fin around 1996 ` and was then given a
OL,11,FSunday morning political discussion
OL,12,Fshow in 1997.
OL,14,F"And later a lunchtime show, where we
OL,15,Fwould get London restaurants to cook a
OL,16,FSunday lunch and bring it in for all
OL,17,Fthe guests to share.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14412
SC,0012
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G12/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"This was followed by a Saturday
OL,7,Fmid-morning show from 1999 to 2003 when
OL,8,FChrysalis bought the station and sacked
OL,9,Fpretty much everyone apart from Nick
OL,10,FFerrari and Steve Allen.
OL,12,F"James O'Brien used to dep for me!"
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14413
SC,0013
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G13/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID THE CHANNEL 4 JOB COME ABOUT
OL,7,GAND MOVE INTO TV?
OL,9,F"Channel 4 was a straightforward advert
OL,10,Fand application.
OL,12,F"I didn't get the job immediately but
OL,13,Fthey had another announcer leaving four
OL,14,Fmonths later and asked me to join for
OL,15,Fthat.
OL,17,F"We were all working on the same floor
OL,18,F` divided into four teams with an
OL,19,Feditor who ran and managed each team in
OL,20,Ffour-week cycles.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14414
SC,0014
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G14/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"We were run by CATS ` Computer Aided
OL,7,FTransmission System ` so we wrote
OL,8,Feverything in advance into that and had
OL,9,Fto make sure we hit certain points such
OL,10,Fas the seven o'clock news junction.
OL,12,F"The computer added up our script
OL,13,Ftimings and we were partly responsible
OL,14,Ffor ensuring everything kept to time
OL,15,Fwithin the script.
OL,17,F"The computer also opened and closed
OL,18,Four microphones ` so woe betide you if
OL,19,Fyou hadn't finished speaking by the
OL,20,Ftime the count in your ear went 'zero'.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14415
SC,0015
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G15/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"We also watched everything beforehand
OL,7,F(everything that was available) on VHS
OL,8,Fto monitor content and be able to write
OL,9,Fin that offbeat C4 style.
OL,11,F"Several of mine got into the
OL,12,Fnewspapers ` including my intro to the
OL,13,FBillionaire Boys Club ('what goes yuppy
OL,14,F` must come down') and an intro to
OL,15,FTreasure Hunt ('what's got a trim
OL,16,Fwaist, two legs and flies ` no not
OL,17,FAnneka Rice ` it's Kenneth Kendall's
OL,18,Ftrousers!') ` which also got reported
OL,19,Fto the duty office by one caller, who
OL,20,Fdescribed it as 'pure smut'!"
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14416
SC,0016
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G16/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GANY MEMORIES OF WORKING IN BBC
OL,7,GPRESENTATION VOICING TRAILS?
OL,9,F"Yes, Deadly (Alan Dedicoat) and I
OL,10,Fvoiced the trailers ` primarily because
OL,11,Fwe sounded pretty similar and had a
OL,12,Fgood range.
OL,14,F"In those days, you'd do a couple of
OL,15,Fdramas, a quiz show, some comedies and
OL,16,Fmaybe a documentary or two all in the
OL,17,Fsame session.
OL,19,F"The flexibility to vary our styles
OL,20,Fmeant we could cover them all off.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14417
SC,0017
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G17/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"I voiced the 1993 BBC Christmas
OL,7,Fcampaign ` three weekends voicing 206
OL,8,Ftrailers.
OL,10,F"The other factor that made them use us
OL,11,Fwas we were very good at repeating what
OL,12,Fwe had just done ` and as we recorded
OL,13,Fon 1" and needed to repeat 5 versions
OL,14,Fof each trailer exactly the same but
OL,15,Fwith a different ending ('next Friday',
OL,16,F'on Friday', 'tomorrow', 'today', 'in
OL,17,Fhalf an hour'), we would make it all
OL,18,Fvery simple and quick.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14418
SC,0018
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G18/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"Once we went digital of course, you
OL,7,Fwould do one version and add five tags
OL,8,Fthat they edited on afterwards. No
OL,9,Fskill required. All recorded in Pres B
OL,10,Fin the afternoon before people like
OL,11,FPhillip Schofield needed to come in and
OL,12,Fdo the broom cupboard."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14419
SC,0019
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G19/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GHOW DID YOU GET THE HOMEWISE JOB AND
OL,7,GWHAT WAS IT LIKE WORKING WITH ANOTHER
OL,8,GWONDERFUL BROADCASTING LEGEND, ANNE
OL,9,GGREGG?
OL,11,F"Homewise was done while I was also
OL,12,Fdoing Radio 5 breakfast. The job was
OL,13,Ffound by my agent.
OL,15,F"But as the reporter on pre-recorded
OL,16,Flocation, I only met Anne once, so I
OL,17,Fcouldn't really tell you. She seemed
OL,18,Fvery pleasant on the one occasion we
OL,19,Fdid meet."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14420
SC,0020
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G20/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GWHAT ARE YOUR MEMORIES OF THE LAUNCH
OL,7,GOF QVC AND WHO WERE THE OTHER LAUNCH
OL,8,GPRESENTERS?
OL,10,F"QVC was tough ` 18 hours of live
OL,11,Funscripted TV a week and no guests (not
OL,12,Flike now where every hour has an
OL,13,Fexpert).
OL,15,F"We had no idea what to expect as it
OL,16,Fwas the first 'selly telly' outside of
OL,17,Fthe US anywhere.
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14421
SC,0021
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G21/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,F"There were seven of us if I remember
OL,7,Fcorrectly ` Julia Roberts (who is still
OL,8,Fthere I believe). who appears on the
OL,9,Flaunch video with me, Paul Lavers, Kara
OL,10,FTritton, Steve Whately, Suzanne Evett
OL,11,Fand Katy John.
OL,13,F"I was the only one with a large amount
OL,14,Fof broadcast experience ` so they gave
OL,15,Fme the first hour and the first product
OL,16,F(a Volkswagen Beetle alarm clock) and
OL,17,Fwe made News at Ten that night. Such
OL,18,Fwas the interest."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14422
SC,0022
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G22/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GWHEN RECORDING THE WEAKEST LINK, WERE
OL,7,GYOU IN THE STUDIO OR IN A SOUND BOOTH?
OL,9,F"We started doing it in a London studio
OL,10,Fas post-production ` and then after
OL,11,Fseries three, I would record the links
OL,12,Fin my own home studio and send them the
OL,13,Ffiles to be edited in."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14423
SC,0023
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F144A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5          G23/25
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with voiceover artist
OL,4,CJon Briggs
OL,5,
OL,6,GANY ANECDOTES OF WHEN THINGS WENT
OL,7,GWRONG DURING YOUR LONG BROADCASTING
OL,8,GCAREER?
OL,10,F"Very early on in my career, aged 17,
OL,11,Fon Timmy Mallet's show, I told a joke
OL,12,Fabout there being a four-letter word at
OL,13,Fthe bottom of my budgie's cage ` to
OL,14,Fwhich Timmy would go ` oh yes what's'
OL,15,Fthat
OL,17,F"The response should have been 'grit' `
OL,18,Fbut somehow that didn't come out and I
OL,19,Fsaid 'sh*t' instead.
OL,21,F"I thought my fledgling broadcast
OL,22,Fcareer was over."
OL,23,EPub: 12-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,145,140,120,200,0,100
